    "key_insight": "The 1919 Colonial Office List represents a TRANSITION PERIOD. Former German colonies captured during WWI are mentioned but NOT YET established as separate League of Nations mandate territories. British Togoland and British Cameroons were being administered as extensions of existing colonies (Gold Coast and Nigeria respectively). Middle Eastern territories (Palestine, Iraq) were still under military administration and had not yet been transferred to Colonial Office control. The formal mandate system would be established in 1920-1922."
